  message: "SECOND PASS, 15 more surveys made fresh on WI-nibav's tree (gin, coredns, alertmanager, ripgrep, hadolint, servant, postal, spring-petclinic, okhttp, fastapi, robyn, cowboy, http4s, howler.js, detekt), same instrument. Two more repos move, both go, both the same under-qualified rows: coredns 10 edges (filepath<-path/filepath Walk 6, grpc<-google.golang.org/grpc NewClient 4), alertmanager 1 (filepath.Glob). Zero diffs in rust, haskell (hadolint, servant), ruby (postal), java (spring-petclinic), kotlin (okhttp, detekt), python (fastapi, robyn), erlang (cowboy), scala (http4s), js (howler.js).\nTOTAL over 44 surveys: 6 repos, 89 tagged edges decided only by the hint-longer direction: go 35 true positives (argo-cd 24, coredns 10, alertmanager 1), c 9 true-by-luck (powerdns sys/time->time), ts 41 false positives (koel @/services/http), python 4 (pretix defusedcsv, now absorbed by its own row). What this does NOT show: any adjudication beyond reading the primitive and the hint; behaviour on repos outside these 44; taint verdict movement (the A/B was io tagging only)."  # 0d43
